 <p>Page-specific excerpts are recorded in the repository review evidence: <a href="https://github.com/burnzoire/oversweep/blob/main/docs/reviews/threat-avoidance-evidence.md">Threat Avoidance evidence</a>. The worked example's flight is invented; its calls follow [3]. Figure 2's numbers are this page's own kinematics, not a source's.</p>
 <p class="note">Applicability: military aircrew of every service, fixed and rotary wing. Two sources are F-16 handbooks and one an Army helicopter manual; their principles are presented generally, and any aircraft's own flight and tactics manuals govern its maneuvers, limits and countermeasures. Detailed threat-specific tactics are classified and are not here. This revision is Drafted pending independent source-backed review.</p>
